\section{Why the address is not optional}{

Keying on the name alone does not work, and the margin is not close.
Measured over 88,744 renderings: 727 of 63,310 bare name keys (1.15\%) carry
more than one EIN, and the worst is \verb{HABITAT FOR HUMANITY} with \strong{39}.
\verb{RONALD MCDONALD HOUSE} has 31, \verb{BIG BROTHERS BIG SISTERS} 29. Adding ZIP5
takes that to \strong{0 of 66,425}. Any \verb{(name_key, zip5)} that still resolves to
more than one EIN is dropped rather than guessed at, and the count is
reported in the \code{ambiguous_dropped} attribute.
}

